# Zero-budget configuration (copy to .env)

Everything below has a free tier or is free outright. Nothing here needs a
credit card. The two things that stay genuinely optional are a domain for the
SMTP identity and a residential proxy — both are marked.

```ini
# ---------- LLM: free tier, with a second provider as fallback ----------
# OpenRouter free models end in ":free" and are rate-limited (roughly 20 req/min,
# provider-dependent daily caps). Groq and Google AI Studio are the usual second
# choice: both give an OpenAI-compatible endpoint and a free quota.
LLM_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
LLM_API_KEY=
LLM_MODEL=

# Tried automatically when the primary returns 429/5xx or keeps failing
LLM_FALLBACK_BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
LLM_FALLBACK_API_KEY=
LLM_FALLBACK_MODEL=

# Keep under the free tier's limits. Raise only after you see 429s stop.
LEADFORGE_LLM_REQUESTS_PER_MINUTE=8
LEADFORGE_LLM_DAILY_CAP=80

# ---------- Proxy: pick ONE free option ----------
# a) Tor (installed locally, no account): slow, many exit nodes are blocked
# LEADFORGE_PROXY_URL=socks5h://127.0.0.1:9050
#
# b) Cloudflare WARP in proxy mode: `warp-cli mode proxy` then this port
# LEADFORGE_PROXY_URL=socks5://127.0.0.1:40000
#
# c) Harvested free list: python scripts/proxy_harvest.py  (then leave URL empty;
#    the router reads data/proxies.txt and rotates)
LEADFORGE_PROXY_URL=
LEADFORGE_PROXY_TIER1=true
LEADFORGE_PROXY_TIER2=true
LEADFORGE_PROXY_TIER3=true

# ---------- SMTP: null sender needs no domain and costs nothing ----------
# `off` = no SMTP at all (pattern evidence only)
# `null_sender` = MAIL FROM:<> probe, no domain of your own required
# `domain` = needs a real address at a domain you control (costs a domain)
LEADFORGE_SMTP_VERIFY_MODE=null_sender
LEADFORGE_SMTP_MAIL_FROM=

# ---------- Search: DuckDuckGo is keyless; SearXNG is local and free ----------
# LEADFORGE_SEARXNG_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8888

# ---------- Browser: headed is free, and the profile stores your session ----------
LEADFORGE_BROWSER_ENABLED=true
LEADFORGE_BROWSER_HEADED=true
LEADFORGE_BROWSER_CHANNEL=chrome
```
